# libpsl -- the Public Suffix List, a hard dependency of libsoup3.
#
# libsoup uses it to decide whether a cookie may be set for a domain: without a
# suffix list, "example.co.uk" and "co.uk" are indistinguishable and a site can
# set a cookie for an entire national registry. libsoup3's meson takes it as
# dependency('libpsl', version : '>=0.20') with no option guard, so this is here
# for gnome-software rather than for flatpak.
#
# Duct's curl is deliberately built --without-libpsl, which is why nothing has
# needed this until now.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
SRC_URL=https://github.com/rockdaboot/libpsl/releases/download/0.21.5/libpsl-0.21.5.tar.gz
SRC_SHA256=1dcc9ceae8b128f3c0b3f654decd0e1e891afc6ff81098f227ef260449dae208
SRC_DIR=libpsl-0.21.5

# --disable-runtime IS THE DECISION IN THIS RECIPE AND IT COSTS A REAL
# CAPABILITY, so it is written down rather than left as an absence.
#
# configure offers --enable-runtime=libidn2|libicu|libidn, DEFAULTING TO AUTO,
# and libidn2 additionally needs libunistring. None of those three is packaged.
# At its default, auto resolves to enable_runtime=no -- the right outcome for the
# wrong reason, and the shape this workstream has named a dozen times.
#
# WHAT IS LOST: run-time IDNA conversion, so libpsl cannot normalise
# internationalised domain names before matching them against the list. An ASCII
# domain is matched correctly; a Unicode one is not converted first. For
# gnome-software talking to Flathub over ASCII hostnames this is invisible, and
# it would matter to a general-purpose browser.
# WHAT IS NOT LOST: the suffix list itself. --enable-builtin generates the PSL
# data into the library, so cookie-domain checking works; only the IDN
# normalisation step is absent.
#
# Named explicitly rather than left at auto so that packaging libidn2 later for
# some other consumer does not silently change what this library does.
#
# --enable-builtin: generate the built-in PSL data rather than relying on a
# system list file that this distribution does not ship.
#
# --disable-gtk-doc and --disable-man: gtk-doc is already off upstream; man
# defaults to auto and needs tooling that is not packaged.
CONFIGURE_ARGS="--disable-static --disable-runtime --enable-builtin \
--disable-gtk-doc --disable-man"
